  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This recording captures Mountain Goats performing on Wednesday, February 25, 2009, at the Swedish American Hall in San Francisco, California [1][3]. Taped by rainingvodka, the 96-minute audio file documents 28 songs from the set [1]. It is the only archived recording of this specific performance and has received a perfect 5/5 rating from one listener [1]. The setlist includes several tracks that are rare or unique to the archive, such as “Any Available Surface,” “Island Garden,” and “Ox Baker Triumphant Intro Story,” which are the only archived performances of those songs [1][3]. Other notable inclusions are “Alphabetizing,” “Billy The Kid's Dream of the Magic Shoes,” and “Ghosts,” all of which are considered bustouts with limited archived history [1][3]. The performance also features well-known tracks like “Jenny,” “This Year,” and “No Children” [1][3]. A listener review of this specific recording describes it as a pivotal live show that turned them into a lifelong fan, praising the quality and the banter [2]. The review highlights the mix of obscure songs, such as “From TG&Y” and “Golden Boy,” alongside classics, noting that fans owe it to themselves to listen [2]. The recording is part of a larger collection of 467 archived shows for the band, with the previous archived show taking place the day before at the Herbst Theatre [3].",
